{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Draw near, carry your brothers</b> — I found in Torat Kohanim in the parashah of the inaugural rites (beginning of Shemini, Leviticus 10:5): Rabbi Eliezer says: the sons of Aharon died only outside, in a place where the Levites are permitted to enter, as it is said: \"and they drew near and carried them in their tunics.\" If so, why is it said \"and they died before HaShem\"? The angel struck them and brought them outside. Rabbi Akiva says: they died only inside, as it is said: \"and they died before HaShem.\" If so, why is it said \"and they drew near and carried them in their tunics\"? They put iron hooks in them and dragged them and brought them outside. Thus far the baraita.\n\nAnd the reason is that although the priests too are forbidden to enter the Sanctuary except during the time of service, that applies only to entering for no purpose, but to remove impurity from there or to inspect the House, one may enter. For thus we learned in Torat Kohanim (Emor, chapter 3, halakhah 11): One might think he may not enter to lay out the cakes? Scripture teaches: \"only\" (Leviticus 21:23). Such is their rule: the priests enter there; if there are no priests — the Levites enter there; if there are no ones who are pure — ones who are impure enter there; if there are no ones who are unblemished — ones who have blemishes enter there. And now, on this day, there were no priests there, for they had been commanded not to defile themselves for them. But since it was possible with hooks and dragging, they were not permitted to enter there.\n\nAnd according to the opinion of Rabbi Eliezer, because Scripture says \"and they drew near,\" he holds that they were outside, and therefore it does not say \"they dragged them in their tunics.\" And the reason for \"in their tunics\" is that they were wearing priestly garments.\n\nNow, Moshe commanded to take them out outside the camp, and there they would strip them of the priestly garments and dress them in burial shrouds and bury them according to their custom like the rest of the dead in the wilderness. And afterward they purified the sacred garments, and they went to the other priests."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The Sifrei Zuta passage in Torat Kohanim references Leviticus 10:5 for the baraita about Shemini; the halakhah citation from Emor refers to Sifra Emor 3:11."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:15.548065904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}